# Example ReRDMFT input file: water, X2C spinors, MULLER JK-only functional, FULL_OPTIMIZATION
# TRUE with ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO -- the NEO counterpart of water_X2C_full_optimization.inp, same
# system, same functional. NEO's Newton steps are restricted to the time-reversal-symmetric
# (Kramers-restricted) subspace (Utils/KramersRestriction.h's KramersNeoProblem), exactly as
# ADAM's own steps are; the validation checks are unchanged (Kramers symmetry of the occupations,
# the gradient and a probe rotation). See water_muller_as_neo_full_optimization.inp for what
# ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO changes in general.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
